A coastal report about waves around a stone pier: an investigation into the effects of waves on a structure and the impact on the surrounding environment
Introduction: Coastal erosion, coastal engineering, wave energy, coastal morphology
The purpose of this report is to investigate the effects of waves on a stone pier and its impact on the surrounding environment. A stone pier is a type of coastal structure that can have significant effects on the local ecosystem and coastal morphology.
The report begins by providing a brief overview of the importance of coastal engineering and the impact of waves on the environment. It then discusses the effects of waves on the structure of the pier, including erosion, wave transmission, and wave reflection.
The report also examines the impact of the pier on the surrounding environment, including changes to the local coastline, the effects on marine life, and the potential impacts on local industries. Finally, the report concludes by discussing the potential benefits and drawbacks of the pier and recommendations for future management